    "question": "Aren’s flight from New York to Hawaii will take 11 hours 20 minutes.  He spends 2 hours reading, 4 hours watching two movies, 30 minutes eating his dinner, 40 minutes listening to the radio, and 1 hour 10 minutes playing games.  How many hours does he have left to take a nap?",
    "gold": "3",
    "answer": "The flight from NY to Hawaii will take 60 x 11 + 20 = <<60*11+20=680>>680 minutes.\nAll the activities will take 120 + 240 + 30 + 40 + 70 = <<120+240+30+40+70=500>>500 minutes.\nFor his nap, he has 680 - 500 = <<680-500=180>>180 minutes.\nTo convert minutes to hours, he has 180/ 60 = <<180/60=3>>3 hours.\n#### 3"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many hours Aren has left to take a nap, we need to first calculate the total time he spends on all his activities and then subtract this from the total flight time.\n\nThe total flight time is 11 hours and 20 minutes. We can convert this time into minutes for easier calculation:\n\\[ 11 \\text{ hours} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes/hour} + 20 \\text{ minutes} = 660 \\text{ minutes} + 20 \\text{ minutes} = 680 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total time Aren spends on his activities:\n- Reading: 2 hours = 2 \\times 60 = 120 \\text{ minutes}\n- Watching movies: 4 hours = 4 \\times 60 = 240 \\text{ minutes}\n- Eating dinner: 30 minutes\n- Listening to the radio: 40 minutes\n- Playing games: 1 hour and 10 minutes = 1 \\times 60 + 10 = 70 \\text{ minutes}\n\nAdding these times together:\n\\[ 120 \\text{ minutes} + 240 \\text{ minutes} + 30 \\text{ minutes} + 40 \\text{ minutes} + 70 \\text{ minutes} = 500 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nNow, we subtract the total time spent on activities from the total flight time:\n\\[ 680 \\text{ minutes} - 500 \\text{ minutes} = 180 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert the remaining time back into hours and minutes:\n\\[ 180 \\text{ minutes} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of hours Aren has left to take a nap is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
